1
00:00:32,762 --> 00:00:38,120
A wave of simultaneous kidnappings
has struck seven cities in Asia!

2
00:00:40,165 --> 00:00:42,344
The incidents happened in Tokyo,

3
00:00:42,498 --> 00:00:45,105
Seoul, Singapore, Bangkok,

4
00:00:45,172 --> 00:00:47,630
Manila, Taipei, and Naha.

5
00:00:47,714 --> 00:00:49,339
Seven cities in total.

6
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:55,839
Red rose petals were found
at the scene of each crime.

7
00:00:56,422 --> 00:01:00,214
Breaking news!
Abductions in seven Asian cities!

8
00:01:40,922 --> 00:01:42,964
KIDNAP GAME

9
00:01:45,297 --> 00:01:49,089
36 HOURS UNTIL THE START OF
KIDNAP GAME

10
00:01:55,282 --> 00:01:59,059
TOKYO

11
00:02:03,672 --> 00:02:06,922
AM 07:02 JST

12
00:02:12,755 --> 00:02:16,005
DETECTIVE
TOSHIRO NIIDE

13
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:27,135
Saori!

14
00:02:33,188 --> 00:02:35,772
You're crushing me.

15
00:02:38,897 --> 00:02:40,272
Oh...

16
00:02:42,563 --> 00:02:44,730
Thanks for waking me.

17
00:02:46,188 --> 00:02:48,556
-What's that?
-I bought it for tomorrow.

18
00:02:50,105 --> 00:02:52,776
Tomorrow? The Tokyo Festival?

19
00:02:53,063 --> 00:02:54,756
No.

20
00:02:55,647 --> 00:02:56,576
Did you forget?

21
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:04,236
No way I'd forget. It's our... tenth.

22
00:03:04,688 --> 00:03:07,772
Our gold anniversary. Wait, silver?

23
00:03:07,843 --> 00:03:11,130
Uh-huh. Your coffee's getting cold.

24
00:03:15,233 --> 00:03:16,690
Thanks for protecting me.

25
00:03:24,188 --> 00:03:26,522
It's bigger than ever this year.

26
00:03:26,688 --> 00:03:31,647
The festivities include a parade
and a greeting from foreign guests.

27
00:03:31,931 --> 00:03:33,780
A large turnout is expected.

28
00:03:34,253 --> 00:03:38,560
Traffic restrictions will be placed around
the venue.

29
00:03:39,064 --> 00:03:43,352
The police will dispatch units
to direct traffic and enhance security.

30
00:03:45,855 --> 00:03:47,813
I wonder if we'll see the fireworks.

31
00:03:48,147 --> 00:03:51,022
The new, big condo might block the view.

32
00:03:51,850 --> 00:03:55,392
No. I mean can we see them together?

33
00:03:57,522 --> 00:03:58,397
Sure we can.

34
00:03:58,778 --> 00:04:00,486
Aren't you on duty?

35
00:04:00,563 --> 00:04:01,688
I am.

36
00:04:01,772 --> 00:04:04,813
But I get off after the parade at five.

37
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,458
It starts at seven, so you'll make it.

38
00:04:13,515 --> 00:04:15,182
Yeah. Delicious, thanks.

39
00:04:17,685 --> 00:04:18,851
What about you?

40
00:04:19,235 --> 00:04:23,522
I think I can get off early,
so I'll cook us a nice dinner.

41
00:04:23,926 --> 00:04:28,343
A nice dinner, huh?
Then could you grab some champagne?

42
00:04:28,905 --> 00:04:33,488
Don't you mean beer?
Hey, I found a delicious craft beer.

43
00:04:34,145 --> 00:04:35,645
Looking forward to it.

44
00:04:39,027 --> 00:04:40,319
That was delicious.

45
00:04:49,333 --> 00:04:51,875
-Well, I'll be off.
-Have a good day.

46
00:04:54,125 --> 00:04:58,708
Grandma? Michiyo?

47
00:04:59,625 --> 00:05:02,666
Mr. Tadokoro, is your wife missing?

48
00:05:02,750 --> 00:05:06,083
Yeah, she's probably lost again.

49
00:05:06,166 --> 00:05:08,125
Did anything unusual happen?

50
00:05:09,886 --> 00:05:12,678
Ah... the bread for breakfast.

51
00:05:13,337 --> 00:05:14,212
Bread?

52
00:05:16,706 --> 00:05:19,915
She said something about
forgetting to buy it.

53
00:05:22,625 --> 00:05:26,125
Mrs. Tadokoro!
Good morning. It's me, Niide.

54
00:05:26,516 --> 00:05:30,058
Your husband's looking for you.
Let's go home.

55
00:05:30,474 --> 00:05:31,891
Okay? Let's go.

56
00:05:31,975 --> 00:05:33,250
That's one thousand yen.

57
00:05:34,094 --> 00:05:36,761
Huh? Ah...

58
00:05:36,931 --> 00:05:42,848
You don't have your wallet... I guess not.

59
00:05:48,208 --> 00:05:49,750
Mind the steps.

60
00:05:53,458 --> 00:05:54,791
Okay, let's go.

61
00:05:57,041 --> 00:06:00,213
-You got bread.
-This bakery is delicious!

62
00:06:00,291 --> 00:06:01,333
Is that so?

63
00:06:01,375 --> 00:06:04,500
FLOWER SHOP
ATRA

64
00:06:07,458 --> 00:06:11,666
SEOUL

65
00:06:14,625 --> 00:06:18,166
AM 08:08 KST

66
00:06:29,291 --> 00:06:32,750
DOCTOR
HAN KIJU

67
00:06:35,708 --> 00:06:42,791
HANDS OF GOD
DOCTOR ENJOYS EASY RETIREMENT

68
00:06:45,166 --> 00:06:49,625
WIFE IS COSMETICS MOGUL
BLIND DAUGHTER IS VIOLIN PRODIGY

69
00:06:52,708 --> 00:06:57,333
ALL BECAUSE OF HIS DAUGHTER'S
FAILED SURGERY?!

70
00:07:07,958 --> 00:07:09,375
Rian?

71
00:07:11,875 --> 00:07:14,041
Let's get ready for school.

72
00:07:14,345 --> 00:07:15,679
I'll take that.

73
00:07:22,755 --> 00:07:23,797
Rian.

74
00:07:24,088 --> 00:07:25,879
It was great. Thanks.

75
00:07:27,039 --> 00:07:28,122
Sure.

76
00:07:30,198 --> 00:07:31,070
Up you go.

77
00:07:41,009 --> 00:07:42,343
Have you read this?

78
00:07:42,901 --> 00:07:44,526
Such a load of garbage.

79
00:07:45,530 --> 00:07:47,000
Don't let it bother you.

80
00:07:47,271 --> 00:07:49,640
They're even sensationalizing Rian.

81
00:07:55,541 --> 00:08:02,541
Rian, about your recital tomorrow...
Mom might not make it.

82
00:08:04,375 --> 00:08:09,458
It can't be helped if Mom is busy.
What about you, Dad?

83
00:08:09,583 --> 00:08:13,125
Me? I'll go for sure.

84
00:08:14,217 --> 00:08:16,424
You won't have an urgent surgery?

85
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:19,252
Don't worry.

86
00:08:19,338 --> 00:08:22,588
There are plenty of other good doctors.

87
00:08:23,557 --> 00:08:27,849
I see.
But don't mind me if they need you, okay?

88
00:08:29,003 --> 00:08:33,128
Your job is to save people's lives,
after all.

89
00:08:36,916 --> 00:08:39,958
Yes, that's right.

90
00:08:52,250 --> 00:08:54,291
FLOWER SHOP
ATRA

91
00:08:57,250 --> 00:09:00,750
SINGAPORE

92
00:09:08,875 --> 00:09:11,958
FLIGHT ATTENDANT
JANICE LAU

93
00:09:13,166 --> 00:09:17,125
Sorry, I'm late.
Got stuck in traffic.

94
00:09:21,284 --> 00:09:22,367
Janice!

95
00:09:25,618 --> 00:09:26,216
Sorry.

96
00:09:27,829 --> 00:09:29,204
He proposed?!

97
00:09:29,329 --> 00:09:31,121
Not yet.

98
00:09:31,204 --> 00:09:33,371
But he did booked
Monti Marina Bay tomorrow.

99
00:09:33,496 --> 00:09:36,788
No way!
You’ve almost got your meal ticket!

100
00:09:36,913 --> 00:09:39,954
What are you talking about?
The meal ticket’s just a bonus.

101
00:09:40,496 --> 00:09:42,871
Tony’s a really sweet guy.

102
00:09:43,805 --> 00:09:46,513
What do you think
I should wear tomorrow?

103
00:09:47,256 --> 00:09:50,214
You know,
I don’t want to overdo it, y’know...

104
00:09:50,246 --> 00:09:54,996
It’s not about clothes.
It’s about showing up on time.

105
00:09:55,913 --> 00:09:59,496
Don’t worry,
I’ll be on time even if it kills me.

106
00:10:04,788 --> 00:10:06,454
FLOWER SHOP
ATRA

107
00:10:09,288 --> 00:10:12,913
BANGKOK

108
00:10:14,163 --> 00:10:16,704
AM 08:46 ICT

109
00:10:17,098 --> 00:10:18,140
Aum.

110
00:10:18,288 --> 00:10:19,329
HOSTESS
AUM THANAWAN

111
00:10:19,454 --> 00:10:21,413
You're still smoking this?

112
00:10:21,663 --> 00:10:23,512
I thought you already quit!

113
00:10:27,292 --> 00:10:29,000
I don't use it anymore.

114
00:10:29,579 --> 00:10:31,621
Then what's this?

115
00:10:34,746 --> 00:10:39,688
Are you still dealing? Why, Aum?!

116
00:10:41,079 --> 00:10:43,247
It's the only way I know how to live!

117
00:10:53,371 --> 00:10:54,746
FLOWER SHOP
ATRA

118
00:10:57,579 --> 00:11:01,038
MANILA

119
00:11:03,216 --> 00:11:06,799
PM 02:07 PHT

120
00:11:08,079 --> 00:11:09,871
TAXI DRIVER
MIGUEL GARCIA

121
00:11:09,967 --> 00:11:14,416
Are you from Japan?

122
00:11:15,129 --> 00:11:17,768
Yeah, we're on our honeymoon.

123
00:11:18,499 --> 00:11:22,915
-Hey, your Japanese is great!
-Thanks.

124
00:11:23,173 --> 00:11:27,673
I used to work in Tokyo.

125
00:11:28,371 --> 00:11:33,514
Have you been to
the Manila Baywalk Dolomite beach?

126
00:11:35,031 --> 00:11:39,364
They say if you see that emerald sea at...

127
00:11:41,246 --> 00:11:47,538
3 p.m, if you see the sea,
your love will last forever.

128
00:11:48,406 --> 00:11:50,656
It doesn’t say that in the guidebook.

129
00:11:51,469 --> 00:11:55,844
It’s veery famous among the youth in Manila.

130
00:11:56,224 --> 00:12:00,258
My 20-year-old granddaughter told me.

131
00:12:01,704 --> 00:12:03,131
-Wow!
-Wow!

132
00:12:03,306 --> 00:12:06,305
-It's so beautiful.
-It really is.

133
00:12:25,788 --> 00:12:27,996
FLOWER SHOP
ATRA

134
00:12:30,871 --> 00:12:34,454
TAIPEI

135
00:12:38,913 --> 00:12:42,121
AM 10:48 TST

136
00:13:02,704 --> 00:13:06,538
HOUSEWIFE
CHRISTINA LIN

137
00:13:09,450 --> 00:13:10,742
What's wrong?

138
00:13:13,154 --> 00:13:14,579
You're not filming again are you?

139
00:13:15,564 --> 00:13:17,806
No! And I deleted the old video.

140
00:13:21,855 --> 00:13:23,314
Don't you believe me?

141
00:13:30,189 --> 00:13:31,189
Christina...

142
00:13:32,814 --> 00:13:33,685
You're my one true love.

143
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,219
I want to be with you.

144
00:13:37,272 --> 00:13:38,385
Don't you trust me?

145
00:13:41,314 --> 00:13:42,091
I do.

146
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:55,772
ATRA
FLOWER SHOP

147
00:13:58,605 --> 00:14:02,355
NAHA

148
00:14:06,064 --> 00:14:09,730
PM 12:49 JST

149
00:14:13,105 --> 00:14:15,980
SYSTEMS ENGINEER
KURANOSUKE HIGA

150
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:19,397
It's ready. I made your favorite.

151
00:14:21,980 --> 00:14:24,022
I told you that we'll eat out.

152
00:14:24,522 --> 00:14:26,355
What for?

153
00:14:29,980 --> 00:14:34,814
Would it be okay
if I invite some old friends over?

154
00:14:34,939 --> 00:14:37,439
Like former co-workers and neighbors.

155
00:14:37,522 --> 00:14:41,564
You think they'll like that?
They'll only resent you.

156
00:14:42,272 --> 00:14:43,314
I miss them.

157
00:14:43,397 --> 00:14:46,397
You're here now! In my world!

158
00:14:46,897 --> 00:14:50,314
Don't you get it?
Your son is a world-famous CEO!

159
00:15:15,230 --> 00:15:17,564
FLOWER SHOP
ATRA

160
00:15:19,939 --> 00:15:22,564
30 HOURS UNTIL THE START OF
KIDNAP GAME

161
00:15:28,314 --> 00:15:29,939
This is the police.

162
00:15:41,814 --> 00:15:42,856
Shut up.

163
00:15:43,802 --> 00:15:48,510
I'm Niide.
Community Safety Division, Shinjuku Central.

164
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:51,864
We got a call about a child screaming.

165
00:15:52,105 --> 00:15:52,855
Get lost.

166
00:15:52,914 --> 00:15:53,872
Hey...

167
00:15:57,432 --> 00:16:00,640
What a jerk.
That's a wife-beater for sure.

168
00:16:11,230 --> 00:16:14,522
-Stop it!
-You shut your mouth!

169
00:16:14,647 --> 00:16:18,855
-Stop it!
-Shut up! Get away from me!

170
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:23,924
My life's a mess because of you!

171
00:16:24,033 --> 00:16:26,158
Stop it, Dad!

172
00:16:26,911 --> 00:16:30,078
Get off, you little shit!

173
00:16:30,296 --> 00:16:32,671
-You piece of shit!
-You okay?

174
00:16:34,630 --> 00:16:36,344
Stop it!

175
00:17:00,257 --> 00:17:01,632
What's the matter?

176
00:17:02,286 --> 00:17:04,749
We can't just leave.

177
00:17:12,955 --> 00:17:16,876
Next, we make an incision
in the dura along the nerve

178
00:17:17,300 --> 00:17:21,550
to expose C3 and give us
a wider surgical field.

179
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:26,620
This allows us to temporarily
clamp the blood vessel,

180
00:17:26,779 --> 00:17:31,529
making it safer to perform
aneurysm clipping and tumor resection.

181
00:17:35,407 --> 00:17:37,396
Dr. Han, thank you for the lecture.

182
00:17:37,979 --> 00:17:38,716
Please.

183
00:17:40,997 --> 00:17:47,039
Have you thought about it?
I'd like you to take on that surgery.

184
00:17:47,290 --> 00:17:51,248
Like I said before,
I have another lecture scheduled.

185
00:17:51,406 --> 00:17:56,198
The patient's a big-shot politician
with pull in the art world.

186
00:17:56,357 --> 00:17:57,982
Think of your daughter.

187
00:17:58,014 --> 00:17:59,639
I'm sorry.

188
00:18:02,172 --> 00:18:03,099
Now if you'll excuse me.

189
00:18:26,321 --> 00:18:28,169
Will she lose her sight?

190
00:18:29,376 --> 00:18:31,335
You said it would succeed.

191
00:18:32,689 --> 00:18:35,105
You said you'd fix her eyes.

192
00:18:50,164 --> 00:18:51,110
Excuse me, Dr. Han?

193
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:57,243
I'm Park Dongkuk, Midum Funeral Services.

194
00:19:01,668 --> 00:19:04,752
Good luck to your daughter for her recital.

195
00:19:07,471 --> 00:19:08,805
Don't look baffled.

196
00:19:09,335 --> 00:19:12,085
I know everything about you, Doctor.

197
00:19:12,216 --> 00:19:15,174
So if you ever need help, let me know.

198
00:19:24,185 --> 00:19:27,602
That probably won't be necessary.

199
00:19:48,059 --> 00:19:50,716
We can't do anything without a warrant.

200
00:20:12,915 --> 00:20:14,540
Police! Open up!

201
00:20:15,393 --> 00:20:16,768
Open up!

202
00:20:17,368 --> 00:20:18,808
I told you to get lost.

203
00:20:18,973 --> 00:20:20,098
Niide!

204
00:20:20,593 --> 00:20:21,759
Hey!

205
00:20:29,147 --> 00:20:31,064
Hyodo! Hold him down!

206
00:20:32,744 --> 00:20:35,827
Get your filthy hands off!

207
00:20:47,895 --> 00:20:51,395
Put your anger aside.
Show your kindness...

208
00:20:52,425 --> 00:20:57,091
Kindness that shields the weak...

209
00:20:57,453 --> 00:21:02,703
That's the right thing to do.

210
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:08,330
-Hyodo.
-Yes.

211
00:21:13,605 --> 00:21:17,598
Come on out. You okay? C'mon.

212
00:21:20,829 --> 00:21:21,850
It's okay now.

213
00:21:23,629 --> 00:21:26,856
You protected your mom.

214
00:21:30,944 --> 00:21:32,083
You did well.

215
00:21:36,367 --> 00:21:38,023
You're not pregnant.

216
00:21:40,271 --> 00:21:41,403
I see.

217
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:45,577
My mistake.

218
00:21:45,859 --> 00:21:49,210
Might be good to get your husband tested.

219
00:21:52,708 --> 00:21:53,343
Okay.

220
00:22:05,601 --> 00:22:08,185
SAORI
NEW MESSAGE

221
00:22:08,310 --> 00:22:10,351
24 HOURS UNTIL THE GAME STARTS

222
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:13,775
"Twenty-four hours until the game starts."

223
00:22:14,376 --> 00:22:16,283
-Niide!
-Coming.

224
00:22:26,792 --> 00:22:28,542
My sincerest apologies.

225
00:22:29,126 --> 00:22:30,334
For what?

226
00:22:31,709 --> 00:22:35,167
For this...

227
00:22:35,792 --> 00:22:39,265
How many times do I have to tell you?

228
00:22:39,290 --> 00:22:40,725
I didn't hit him.

229
00:22:40,751 --> 00:22:45,001
Damn right you didn't!
You think we're in the seventies?!

230
00:22:45,251 --> 00:22:46,917
But sir, you also...

231
00:22:47,542 --> 00:22:50,209
-Huh?
-Er, nothing.

232
00:22:53,626 --> 00:22:56,584
Well, now you're outta my hair.

233
00:23:00,159 --> 00:23:01,076
Transferal?

234
00:23:01,209 --> 00:23:03,584
ASSIGNED TO HOMICIDE DIVISION

235
00:23:08,398 --> 00:23:09,648
NISHI-SHINJUKU MEDICAL CENTER

236
00:23:09,834 --> 00:23:13,726
-Take care.
-You too.

237
00:23:16,751 --> 00:23:20,220
Might be good to get your husband tested.

238
00:23:31,242 --> 00:23:34,242
-Yes?
-Sorry, I'll be late tonight.

239
00:23:35,786 --> 00:23:40,075
Are you going somewhere?
There's something I'd like to talk about.

240
00:23:40,626 --> 00:23:43,292
I got transferred to the Homicide Division.

241
00:23:44,051 --> 00:23:48,176
The Homicide Division? That's great!

242
00:23:48,278 --> 00:23:50,542
-Niide, let's go!
-Okay.

243
00:23:50,626 --> 00:23:53,458
Saori! We're borrowing Niide!

244
00:23:54,159 --> 00:23:55,659
They want to celebrate.

245
00:23:56,434 --> 00:23:59,559
Can't do without the guest of honor.

246
00:24:00,172 --> 00:24:01,438
Sorry. Bye.

247
00:24:07,332 --> 00:24:08,124
Congratulations.

248
00:24:14,459 --> 00:24:17,092
Tonight, we're here to celebrate...

249
00:24:17,126 --> 00:24:19,667
Cheers!

250
00:24:20,001 --> 00:24:21,876
You just had to, huh?

251
00:24:21,959 --> 00:24:25,636
Niide, let's drink till we drop!

252
00:24:25,975 --> 00:24:27,184
Got it.

253
00:24:27,242 --> 00:24:29,284
-Cheers.
-Cheers. Thanks.

254
00:24:31,714 --> 00:24:35,256
-You drank waaay too much.
-I'm not drunk.

255
00:24:35,686 --> 00:24:38,352
Stairs ahead. Turning here.

256
00:24:40,001 --> 00:24:42,501
-We're boarding.
-Wait a sec...

257
00:24:42,546 --> 00:24:45,129
-Whoa, whoa.
-We're boarding.

258
00:25:04,959 --> 00:25:06,209
Oh, sorry.

259
00:25:19,167 --> 00:25:20,459
Excuse me...

260
00:25:21,959 --> 00:25:23,870
Do you know the trolley problem?

261
00:25:25,584 --> 00:25:26,343
Huh?

262
00:25:27,934 --> 00:25:29,229
The trolley problem.

263
00:25:31,284 --> 00:25:37,796
The one about
the uncontrollable trolley on the rails?

264
00:25:38,664 --> 00:25:39,664
Yes.

265
00:25:40,351 --> 00:25:42,934
If the trolley runs straight,

266
00:25:43,123 --> 00:25:47,392
five workers on the track ahead die.

267
00:25:47,470 --> 00:25:52,345
If you press a button
to divert it to save those five,

268
00:25:52,417 --> 00:25:57,501
one different worker on the other track dies.

269
00:25:58,209 --> 00:26:02,626
Now, if you were there,
would you press that button?

270
00:26:05,459 --> 00:26:12,167
I think...
I'd try to save the five some other way.

271
00:26:12,858 --> 00:26:14,733
Interesting...

272
00:26:15,648 --> 00:26:19,523
Then let's change the rules a bit.

273
00:26:20,127 --> 00:26:23,607
Say there's one person straight ahead,

274
00:26:23,874 --> 00:26:28,082
and five on the other line.

275
00:26:28,338 --> 00:26:32,338
And all you can do
is press the button, or not.

276
00:26:34,125 --> 00:26:39,345
And what if the solo person is...

277
00:26:41,186 --> 00:26:42,561
your wife.

278
00:26:46,644 --> 00:26:49,394
Would you kill the five?

279
00:26:56,721 --> 00:27:01,340
I guess it's hard to answer
a question like that out of the blue.

280
00:27:03,143 --> 00:27:04,268
Yeah.

281
00:27:06,098 --> 00:27:11,931
But there'll come a day
when you have to decide.

282
00:27:30,204 --> 00:27:32,204
See you around, Detective.

283
00:27:33,721 --> 00:27:36,346
"Detective?" Hey, wait...

284
00:28:44,346 --> 00:28:47,235
The person I admire the most is my dad.

285
00:28:47,754 --> 00:28:49,852
He is a doctor.

286
00:28:50,387 --> 00:28:53,663
My dad's job is saving people's lives.

287
00:28:54,093 --> 00:28:58,556
I want to become someone who can
save people, just like him.

288
00:29:32,846 --> 00:29:34,346
I'm home.

289
00:29:50,861 --> 00:29:54,254
You weren't always this studious.
Did you decide on a goal?

290
00:29:55,614 --> 00:29:57,614
Yeah, police officer.

291
00:29:58,108 --> 00:30:00,275
Huh, I wouldn't have guessed.

292
00:30:00,739 --> 00:30:03,660
Did you decide to do
what's right for society?

293
00:30:07,929 --> 00:30:11,370
I think Mom had an unhappy life.

294
00:30:13,503 --> 00:30:16,921
I'm not so sure. She had you, after all.

295
00:30:17,429 --> 00:30:21,637
It was because of me
that she couldn't leave that jerk.

296
00:30:24,066 --> 00:30:27,123
I couldn't protect her.

297
00:30:34,637 --> 00:30:38,762
This is Carrot-Man.
He's kind of a... good-luck charm.

298
00:30:39,096 --> 00:30:40,762
Feel free to throw him out.

299
00:30:41,637 --> 00:30:43,054
Why a carrot?

300
00:30:43,596 --> 00:30:47,804
Your short fuse is because
you don't eat enough carrots.

301
00:30:48,290 --> 00:30:49,207
Irrelevant.

302
00:30:50,038 --> 00:30:53,621
Promise Carrot-Man that you won't get angry.

303
00:30:54,196 --> 00:30:55,112
No.

304
00:30:55,368 --> 00:30:56,660
So you don’t want him?

305
00:30:56,846 --> 00:30:59,248
No... I'll keep him.

306
00:31:02,280 --> 00:31:03,446
Thanks.

307
00:31:10,762 --> 00:31:14,012
Ah, they're starting. Let's go.

308
00:31:17,971 --> 00:31:19,387
What?

309
00:31:32,304 --> 00:31:35,804
-So pretty.
-Awesome.

310
00:31:40,528 --> 00:31:41,861
Let's do this again.

311
00:31:43,412 --> 00:31:46,037
-Next year?
-Yes, next year.

312
00:31:46,221 --> 00:31:47,971
And the year after.

313
00:31:48,183 --> 00:31:53,933
Yeah. Every year, together.

314
00:31:57,608 --> 00:32:00,525
We'll watch them together every year.

315
00:32:47,554 --> 00:32:56,471
12 HOURS UNTIL THE START OF
KIDNAP GAME

316
00:32:56,596 --> 00:33:00,721
TOKYO FESTIVAL 2026

317
00:33:00,804 --> 00:33:05,650
Welcome to TOKYO FESTIVAL.
Parade starts at 10 AM. Fireworks at 7 PM.

318
00:33:10,702 --> 00:33:13,455
What a turnout.

319
00:33:14,247 --> 00:33:16,039
Lot of tourists, too.

320
00:33:16,955 --> 00:33:20,205
And VIPs from all over the world.

321
00:33:20,289 --> 00:33:21,330
VIPs?

322
00:33:21,414 --> 00:33:23,788
Mic test, mic test. One, two, three.

323
00:33:24,120 --> 00:33:25,247
-How is it?
-Okay.

324
00:33:25,417 --> 00:33:26,368
Thank you.

325
00:33:31,816 --> 00:33:33,066
Excuse me.

326
00:33:35,772 --> 00:33:36,794
Hello?

327
00:33:37,201 --> 00:33:40,921
Akina? Sorry, I'll call back if you're busy.

328
00:33:40,992 --> 00:33:42,784
It's fine. What's up?

329
00:33:44,419 --> 00:33:46,336
It's just about Toshiro.

330
00:33:46,432 --> 00:33:48,474
What did he do this time?

331
00:33:49,534 --> 00:33:53,534
No, he's been transferred
to the Homicide Division.

332
00:33:53,619 --> 00:33:58,243
Huh? So his dream has come true at last.
That's fantastic.

333
00:33:59,416 --> 00:34:00,303
Thanks.

334
00:34:00,735 --> 00:34:03,902
But he's gonna get even busier, isn't he?

335
00:34:04,987 --> 00:34:09,403
You haven't told him
about the test yet, right?

336
00:34:10,713 --> 00:34:12,497
Well... no.

337
00:34:12,580 --> 00:34:17,622
How's holding back gonna help?
Think about yourself for a change.

338
00:34:19,039 --> 00:34:22,789
Sorry, there's a patient. I'll call you back.

339
00:34:23,872 --> 00:34:25,747
Is everything okay?

340
00:34:26,747 --> 00:34:28,039
Huh?

341
00:34:30,048 --> 00:34:31,673
-He's all yours.
-Okay.

342
00:34:31,830 --> 00:34:33,455
Take care.

343
00:34:34,205 --> 00:34:36,330
Take your time.

344
00:34:37,839 --> 00:34:39,889
-Hey there.
-Hello.

345
00:34:39,914 --> 00:34:42,622
Have you had lunch?
I've got one left.

346
00:34:42,845 --> 00:34:45,179
-Can I buy that?
-Sure can!

347
00:34:45,686 --> 00:34:47,477
I'll knock 200 yen off.

348
00:34:48,016 --> 00:34:49,014
You're too kind.

349
00:34:54,904 --> 00:34:56,279
I LOVE YOU MOMMY

350
00:34:56,437 --> 00:34:59,228
Is that by your... daughter?

351
00:35:01,284 --> 00:35:06,456
Yup. My pride and joy.
Cute as a button, unlike me.

352
00:35:07,409 --> 00:35:11,617
She's my reason for living.
My whole life, even.

353
00:35:14,366 --> 00:35:15,449
I'm jealous.

354
00:35:16,191 --> 00:35:18,056
Of course, it's not all easy.

355
00:35:24,663 --> 00:35:30,288
That van was also there yesterday.
I wonder what it is.

356
00:35:31,192 --> 00:35:34,609
A florist, perhaps?

357
00:35:36,617 --> 00:35:38,201
Maybe a coincidence.

358
00:35:41,784 --> 00:35:44,367
FLOWER SHOP
ATRA

359
00:36:03,018 --> 00:36:04,579
What's the occasion?

360
00:36:05,379 --> 00:36:09,159
I want to give my daughter a bouquet.

361
00:36:09,826 --> 00:36:11,326
Come on in.

362
00:36:16,064 --> 00:36:18,112
How about something like this?

363
00:36:22,701 --> 00:36:27,205
Wow, they're distinctive.
Would a kid like these?

364
00:36:27,663 --> 00:36:33,163
They have a unique fragrance.
I'm sure your daughter will appreciate them.

365
00:36:35,576 --> 00:36:36,909
Oh, yes.

366
00:36:38,367 --> 00:36:41,034
How do you know she's blind?

367
00:36:47,451 --> 00:36:49,409
That's a message from us.

368
00:36:50,784 --> 00:36:52,659
THE GAME BEGINS IN 5 HOURS.

369
00:36:54,451 --> 00:36:55,909
What's...

370
00:37:06,703 --> 00:37:08,870
Welcome. Can I help you?

371
00:37:10,992 --> 00:37:14,159
The other shop assistant...

372
00:37:15,618 --> 00:37:18,368
I'm the only one working here.

373
00:37:35,365 --> 00:37:36,365
Niide.

374
00:37:37,348 --> 00:37:39,967
-A VIP will pass Point A shortly.
-Okay.

375
00:37:40,212 --> 00:37:42,296
-Be on alert.
-Yes, sir.

376
00:37:42,971 --> 00:37:44,262
Hi, guys.

377
00:37:44,346 --> 00:37:46,137
Good to see you.

378
00:37:46,221 --> 00:37:48,137
They got you on security?

379
00:37:48,221 --> 00:37:51,637
You Community Safety guys don't have it easy.

380
00:37:52,054 --> 00:37:55,346
Niide got transferred to
the Homicide Division.

381
00:37:55,429 --> 00:37:56,804
So I heard.

382
00:37:56,887 --> 00:37:59,080
Congrats. Saori was delighted.

383
00:37:59,929 --> 00:38:02,554
It's your wedding anniversary, too.

384
00:38:02,637 --> 00:38:05,346
Just go back to your post.

385
00:38:08,799 --> 00:38:12,049
And? What did you get for her?

386
00:38:12,262 --> 00:38:13,721
-Huh?
-Huh?

387
00:38:14,346 --> 00:38:16,346
You didn't get her anything?

388
00:38:16,679 --> 00:38:21,012
Don't you know you only
made it this far thanks to her?

389
00:38:21,387 --> 00:38:23,387
Of course, I'm grateful.

390
00:38:26,554 --> 00:38:28,762
You know what's troubling her?

391
00:38:29,679 --> 00:38:30,846
Kinda...

392
00:38:31,637 --> 00:38:34,179
I think you need to address that.

393
00:38:36,054 --> 00:38:37,137
Yeah.

394
00:38:44,596 --> 00:38:48,304
Excuse me. Do you have Hoshikuzu beer?

395
00:38:48,387 --> 00:38:51,096
I'm sorry, we don't stock that.

396
00:38:51,596 --> 00:38:53,262
I see. Thank you.

397
00:38:53,887 --> 00:38:58,221
We're done, but keep an eye out.
I'll notify you on pullout.

398
00:38:58,304 --> 00:38:59,221
Yes, sir.

399
00:38:59,471 --> 00:39:01,346
-Niide.
-Yes.

400
00:39:01,429 --> 00:39:04,387
Could you see the guests to their car?

401
00:39:05,054 --> 00:39:07,637
But I'm off-duty now, sir.

402
00:39:07,721 --> 00:39:11,846
Come on... take one for your old team.

403
00:39:12,762 --> 00:39:14,637
All right, sir.

404
00:39:28,096 --> 00:39:29,929
MUSIC ACHIEVEMENT SHOWCASE

405
00:39:30,012 --> 00:39:33,471
DONGHAE ARTS CENTER

406
00:39:34,179 --> 00:39:36,429
-This way.
-Thank you.

407
00:39:42,512 --> 00:39:44,304
Rian, your dad's here.

408
00:39:51,387 --> 00:39:52,512
Rian.

409
00:39:52,929 --> 00:39:54,221
Dad!

410
00:39:56,679 --> 00:39:59,137
You look lovely.

411
00:40:00,012 --> 00:40:01,554
This is for you.

412
00:40:05,804 --> 00:40:09,679
Thanks. They smell nice.

413
00:40:17,554 --> 00:40:25,054
Mom... really wanted to come,
but she had too much work.

414
00:40:25,762 --> 00:40:26,971
That's a shame, huh

415
00:40:28,679 --> 00:40:32,179
It's okay. You made it.

416
00:40:37,405 --> 00:40:40,523
You know, I can see it.

417
00:40:44,029 --> 00:40:47,975
No matter where, no matter when,
I can see your smile, Dad.

418
00:41:10,159 --> 00:41:13,243
Thank you.

419
00:41:28,846 --> 00:41:33,429
1 HOUR UNTIL THE START OF
KIDNAP GAME

420
00:42:07,554 --> 00:42:08,721
Niide.

421
00:42:09,332 --> 00:42:12,647
I'll write the report. Please, go home.

422
00:42:12,773 --> 00:42:14,689
I owe you one. Thanks.

423
00:42:16,364 --> 00:42:17,905
Welcome.

424
00:42:26,935 --> 00:42:30,227
The language... of flowers...

425
00:42:33,637 --> 00:42:35,721
"Together forever."

426
00:42:38,555 --> 00:42:41,347
"You are perfect."

427
00:42:42,558 --> 00:42:44,558
"Dearest."

428
00:42:46,564 --> 00:42:48,105
This is it.

429
00:42:48,612 --> 00:42:50,987
Can I get eleven white roses?

430
00:43:00,012 --> 00:43:01,429
Found it.

431
00:43:42,510 --> 00:43:47,144
Well, you had everyone transfixed today.

432
00:43:47,356 --> 00:43:48,898
You were like an angel.

433
00:43:49,021 --> 00:43:50,855
-Really?
-Yup.

434
00:43:51,547 --> 00:43:53,589
I wish Mom could have seen.

435
00:43:53,923 --> 00:43:57,596
I'll be sure to bring Mom next time, okay?

436
00:43:57,912 --> 00:43:58,995
Okay.

437
00:44:02,070 --> 00:44:03,237
Just a sec.

438
00:44:06,012 --> 00:44:09,116
EMERGENCY. CALL BACK AT ONCE.

439
00:44:12,852 --> 00:44:14,977
Uh, Rian, just a sec.

440
00:44:19,497 --> 00:44:21,289
Up we go.

441
00:44:23,298 --> 00:44:28,507
I just have to make
a quick call to the hospital.

442
00:44:28,858 --> 00:44:31,858
-Can you wait for me here?
-Okay.

443
00:45:10,887 --> 00:45:14,679
This is Han Kiju.
I got a message about an emergency.

444
00:45:15,212 --> 00:45:18,337
Ah, Dr. Han. I'll check right away.

445
00:45:18,865 --> 00:45:20,143
Please do.

446
00:45:28,311 --> 00:45:30,227
Sorry to keep you waiting.

447
00:45:31,745 --> 00:45:33,079
Oh, it's fine.

448
00:45:56,198 --> 00:45:59,198
SORRY, RUNNING A BIT LATE

449
00:46:00,221 --> 00:46:05,012
1 MINUTE UNTIL THE START OF
KIDNAP GAME

450
00:46:09,136 --> 00:46:13,322
I'm telling you, I got a message
about an emergency.

451
00:46:13,467 --> 00:46:17,842
But nobody here says they sent the message.

452
00:46:20,179 --> 00:46:21,596
What on earth...?

453
00:46:29,713 --> 00:46:31,338
What pretty flowers.

454
00:46:34,907 --> 00:46:36,782
Thank you.

455
00:46:39,505 --> 00:46:44,172
Doesn't this smell nice too?

456
00:46:45,221 --> 00:46:48,563
30 SECONDS UNTIL THE START OF
KIDNAP GAME

457
00:46:53,270 --> 00:46:58,353
What color do you think this rose is?

458
00:47:01,490 --> 00:47:03,184
Red?

459
00:47:03,209 --> 00:47:04,292
No.

460
00:47:05,815 --> 00:47:06,848
It's black.

461
00:47:08,608 --> 00:47:09,858
It's a black rose.

462
00:47:19,367 --> 00:47:22,117
SORRY, RUNNING A BIT LATE

463
00:47:54,554 --> 00:47:57,696
And now it's time for the main event.

464
00:47:58,307 --> 00:48:00,298
In a few moments,

465
00:48:00,330 --> 00:48:05,455
the fireworks bearing our hopes and dreams
will light up the sky.

466
00:48:06,557 --> 00:48:11,890
Now let's bring the Tokyo night sky to life
with the ultimate countdown!

467
00:48:16,814 --> 00:48:19,022
Here we go!

468
00:48:19,185 --> 00:48:25,435
Ten! Nine! Eight! Seven! Six!

469
00:48:25,814 --> 00:48:26,939
Five!

470
00:48:27,022 --> 00:48:28,231
Four!

471
00:48:28,314 --> 00:48:29,647
Three!

472
00:48:29,731 --> 00:48:30,647
Two!

473
00:48:30,731 --> 00:48:32,606
One!

474
00:49:43,522 --> 00:49:44,689
Rian?

475
00:49:46,606 --> 00:49:47,606
Rian!

476
00:49:49,772 --> 00:49:50,856
Rian!

477
00:51:06,272 --> 00:51:07,439
Saori?

478
00:51:28,897 --> 00:51:30,356
Something happen?

479
00:51:31,522 --> 00:51:35,147
-She saw a kidnapping.
-Tell us what you remember.

480
00:51:35,272 --> 00:51:37,314
-I saw...
-Mrs. Tadokoro.

481
00:51:38,064 --> 00:51:39,397
Your wife!

482
00:51:39,772 --> 00:51:43,064
I saw a florist take your wife away!

483
00:51:43,439 --> 00:51:46,022
-Huh?
-I really saw it!

484
00:51:50,981 --> 00:51:52,189
Pause it.

485
00:51:53,223 --> 00:51:54,723
That's Saori.

486
00:51:56,240 --> 00:51:57,566
Please play it.

487
00:52:04,505 --> 00:52:06,547
That's Saori. My wife.

488
00:52:06,622 --> 00:52:08,751
Code red! Track down the van.

489
00:52:08,776 --> 00:52:09,735
Yes, sir.

490
00:52:12,856 --> 00:52:15,981
-You said it was a florist.
-My wife did.

491
00:52:16,661 --> 00:52:19,286
Yes! This is the van.

492
00:52:19,363 --> 00:52:22,363
It turned right at the tee.

493
00:52:29,356 --> 00:52:34,788
Rian can't see.
She wouldn't go home on her own!

494
00:52:34,887 --> 00:52:36,220
Please calm down.

495
00:52:36,266 --> 00:52:38,932
How do you expect me to calm down?!

496
00:52:42,505 --> 00:52:46,921
It was a woman.

497
00:52:49,704 --> 00:52:52,662
She left these rose petals behind.

498
00:52:56,857 --> 00:53:01,357
Have any of you seen my daughter?

499
00:53:01,857 --> 00:53:03,815
Have none of you seen her?

500
00:53:04,831 --> 00:53:10,164
My daughter is about... about this tall...

501
00:53:10,189 --> 00:53:12,914
She's wearing a white coat.

502
00:53:12,939 --> 00:53:14,814
If anyone has seen her, please tell me!

503
00:53:18,731 --> 00:53:22,147
Stand back, stand back.
Please make way.

504
00:53:24,439 --> 00:53:26,689
-Make way.
-Coming through.

505
00:53:40,269 --> 00:53:42,781
-Here's a copy of the map.
-Thanks.

506
00:53:42,806 --> 00:53:45,722
They can't be far.
Hyodo, where's the van?

507
00:53:45,891 --> 00:53:46,974
Um, I don't...

508
00:53:47,038 --> 00:53:49,872
-Use the N System, goddammit!
-Calm down!

509
00:53:50,962 --> 00:53:53,962
Don't forget, you're a part to this, so...

510
00:53:53,987 --> 00:53:55,737
I know that!

511
00:53:56,372 --> 00:53:58,539
She's my wife!

512
00:53:59,553 --> 00:54:01,012
That's why I...

513
00:54:01,095 --> 00:54:02,345
Hold on.

514
00:54:02,720 --> 00:54:08,176
You know it's standard procedure to wait
for the demands in a missing persons case.

515
00:54:08,887 --> 00:54:12,843
The SIT is taking over.
There are press controls in place.

516
00:54:14,095 --> 00:54:15,630
Your job is to cooperate.

517
00:54:27,470 --> 00:54:29,220
AKINA ISOBE

518
00:54:33,553 --> 00:54:34,345
Hello?

519
00:54:34,527 --> 00:54:36,014
I heard about Saori.

520
00:54:36,690 --> 00:54:37,856
I can't talk.

521
00:54:37,881 --> 00:54:41,006
Listen!
Watch the video I'm sending you.

522
00:54:45,470 --> 00:54:46,678
Breaking news.

523
00:54:46,762 --> 00:54:51,512
There is still an uproar
outside this concert hall in Seoul.

524
00:54:51,595 --> 00:54:55,303
An 11-year-old girl who
performed just hours before

525
00:54:55,387 --> 00:54:58,095
has been kidnapped by an unknown party.

526
00:54:58,178 --> 00:54:59,303
South Korea?

527
00:54:59,387 --> 00:55:03,470
The despicable crime was
swiftly committed amid a crowd.

528
00:55:03,553 --> 00:55:07,512
-What's this?
-A girl was kidnapped in Seoul.

529
00:55:07,595 --> 00:55:10,512
-At the same time as Saori.
-So what?

530
00:55:10,595 --> 00:55:17,053
People in other Asian cities were kidnapped
at the same time as Saori, too.

531
00:55:17,303 --> 00:55:19,095
Even the same rose petals.

532
00:55:21,887 --> 00:55:26,053
In Singapore, a man was
